# ── Model (inference) — configure ONE backend ────────────────────────────────
# Option A: Foundry model (BYOK via Managed Identity). Endpoint is auto-injected
# when hosted; only needed locally.
# FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>
# AZURE_AI_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=gpt-4o

# Option B: GitHub Copilot model (fine-grained PAT with Copilot Requests → Read-only).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# ── GitHub resource access ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both protocols start a session-owned stdio MCP server. It resolves the App
# installation for each owner/repository and mints repository- and
# permission-scoped tokens internally.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# Store the PEM contents in Key Vault and set only its secret URI.
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_SECRET_URI=https://<vault>.vault.azure.net/secrets/issuelens-github-app-key

# Wiki routing is configured in the source project's .github/issuelens.yml via
# instructions.team_memory.wiki_repository, not an environment setting.
# It defaults to the source project's own wiki; no per-repository App settings
# or user environment flags are needed. The parent supplies the writer mode.
# Wiki Git operations use the packaged Dulwich Python library, not git.exe or
# a Git/SSH/credential-helper subprocess. No Git installation, Dockerfile change,
# or runtime installer is needed; the host still starts the Python stdio MCP process.
# Requires an initialized destination wiki and App installation there
# with Contents: read/write for the operation. Source-user authorization is
# separate from destination App access; policy alone never authorizes a write.

# ── Foundry toolbox (non-GitHub chat capabilities) ──────────────────────────
# The toolbox must not contain a GitHub MCP connection. GitHub access uses only
# the bundled stdio server above.
# TOOLBOX_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>/toolboxes/<toolbox>/versions/<version>/mcp?api-version=v1

# ── Notifications ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logic App HTTP endpoints for sending notifications. Each enables the matching
# in-process tool (send-email / send-teams-notification) only when set. These
# URLs contain a SAS signature — treat them as secrets.
# MAILING_URL=https://prod-XX.<region>.logic.azure.com:443/workflows/.../triggers/manual/paths/invoke?api-version=2016-10-01&sp=...&sig=...
# PERSONAL_NOTIFICATION_URL=https://prod-XX.<region>.logic.azure.com:443/workflows/.../triggers/manual/paths/invoke?api-version=2016-10-01&sp=...&sig=...
# Default email recipients for the triage report (comma-separated). Optional —
# the send-email tool falls back to this when no recipients are provided.
# RECIPIENTS=alice@contoso.com,bob@contoso.com
